# SehatFlow: Patient Identification, Medical Record Access, Retention Policy and Compliance Audit

## ROLE

Act as a senior healthcare software architect, Android/full-stack engineer, database engineer, QA lead, and privacy-compliance analyst familiar with Indian healthcare software.

SehatFlow is a clinic appointment, queue, and token-management application. It has separate experiences for patients, doctors, receptionists (front desk), and clinic administrators.

The application has previously undergone UAT remediation and security hardening. Inspect the actual repository and existing reports before changing anything.

Your mission is to implement the six requirements below, audit the existing application against them, verify the applicable Indian legal requirements using authoritative sources, fix identified defects, and run regression tests.

**Do not stop after generating a plan or compliance report. Implement the required changes in the existing codebase.**

Do not assume that previous security reports are correct without verifying the current implementation.

