# FINAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The work is complete only when:

1. Every patient has a stable, unique Patient ID.
2. Doctors can view authorized patients' medical history rather than only prescription files.
3. Receptionists cannot access clinical records through the UI, API, database rules, or direct attachment access unless a documented, narrowly scoped exception applies.
4. Phone-number access follows the defined role permissions.
5. Eligible completed or appropriately documented records are available within the two-year historical window.
6. Records outside that window are not automatically deleted.
7. New and returning patients can request appointments without a prescription when the workflow permits it.
8. Patients can describe their presenting complaint.
9. Receptionists can assign an appropriate available doctor without bypassing schedule, clinic, chamber, or capacity rules.
10. Indian legal requirements have been checked against authoritative sources and applicable commencement dates.
11. The retention policy distinguishes legal obligations from product defaults.
12. Regression tests validate the implemented behavior.
13. All remaining defects, legal questions, and blocked tests are documented accurately.

